# Resolve packages from the public npm registry.
#
# Without this, an install inherits whatever registry the machine's user-level
# .npmrc points at. On the machine this project is developed on that is a
# corporate proxy, which bakes internal feed hostnames and SHA-1 integrity
# hashes into pnpm-lock.yaml -- neither of which belongs in a public repository
# that anyone should be able to build.
#
# A repo-level .npmrc takes precedence over the user-level one, so this keeps
# the lockfile portable regardless of who runs the install.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
